    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the build is green. The only test class with `@Test` methods is `AcceptanceTest`, and both its tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key to `SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))` and rewired duplicate detection around it.\n\n**New file**\n- `OwnerSoundex.java` \u2014 a package-private American Soundex helper (`letter + 3 digits`, standard consonant mapping, vowels separating repeats, `h`/`w` non-separating). Used for both the identity key and the soft-match.\n\n**Changed files**\n- `OwnerIdentityKey.java` \u2014 `of(...)` now returns the lower-case 64-char SHA-256 hex digest of `<normalizedTelephone>|<lowerEmail>|<soundex(lastName)>`; `of(Owner)` feeds telephone/email/**lastName** (no longer householdId).\n- `CheckUniqueOwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 the single 409 check now compares the new identity key; the `householdId` derivation was dropped. Still skips soft-deleted owners; the disposable-email blocklist step still runs before it in the pipeline (unchanged YAML).\n- `AssignOwnerPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 soft match now fires when **identityKey differs** but **soundex(lastName)** and **postcode** match (previously exact lastName + postcode + different telephone). `sharesHousehold`/null-postcode guards retained.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 updated the `identityKey` schema description and example to the SHA-256/soundex form.\n\n**Behaviour outcomes (per spec)**\n- Duplicate (409) is now solely the single identity key; the separate computed-`householdId` household-duplicate block is gone (`householdId` is still assigned and used only for `householdSize`/`membershipLevel`).\n- Two owners with the same last name and postcode but **different telephones** now get different keys \u2192 no 409; they match on soundex + postcode \u2192 flagged as a **soft** possible-duplicate instead.\n- Deleted owners are still ignored; the email-domain blocklist still applies first.\n\n`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
